{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":18,"code":"JOB","name":"Job","testament":"OT"},"chapter":26,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"JOB 26:1"},"But Job answered and said, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"JOB 26:2"},"How hast thou helped ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["him that is"]}," without power? ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["how "]},"savest thou the arm ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that hath"]}," no strength? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"JOB 26:3"},"How hast thou counseled ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["him that hath"]}," no wisdom? and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["how"]}," hast thou plentifully declared the thing as it is? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"JOB 26:4"},"To whom hast thou uttered words? and whose spirit came from thee? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"JOB 26:5"},"Dead ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["things"]}," are formed from under the waters, and the inhabitants thereof. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"JOB 26:6"},"Hell ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," naked before him, and destruction hath no covering. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"JOB 26:7"},"He stretcheth out the north over the empty place, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," hangeth the earth upon nothing. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"JOB 26:8"},"He bindeth up the waters in his thick clouds; and the cloud is not rent under them. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"JOB 26:9"},"He holdeth back the face of his throne, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," spreadeth his cloud upon it. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"JOB 26:10"},"He hath compassed the waters with bounds, until the day and night come to an end. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"JOB 26:11"},"The pillars of heaven tremble and are astonished at his reproof. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"JOB 26:12"},"He divideth the sea with his power, and by his understanding he smiteth through the proud. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"JOB 26:13"},"By his spirit he hath garnished the heavens; his hand hath formed the crooked serpent. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"JOB 26:14"},"Lo, these ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," parts of his ways: but how little a portion is heard of him? but the thunder of his power who can understand? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 26:14"}]}]}
